{"id": "xbenin", "name": "Pendjari National Park", "short": "Pendjari", "place": "Benin", "lat": 11.3, "lon": 1.5, "side": "r", "cont": "Africa", "country": "Benin", "kind": "Grassland", "park": true, "blurb": "Savanna grass, kob and elephants, and West Africa's last big lion stronghold.", "tip": {"id": "fire", "title": "Take away fire", "text": "Dry-season fire shapes the savanna. Set Fire to -100% and watch the grasses, then the grazers and the lions that depend on them."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Pendjari National Park", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pendjari_National_Park"}, {"title": "UNESCO: W-Arly-Pendjari Complex", "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/749/"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: W-Arly-Pendjari Complex", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/W-Arly-Pendjari_Complex"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Pendjari National Park", "icon": "lion", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "gayanus", "sp": "andropogon gayanus", "xh": 0.15}, {"id": "diospyros", "sp": "diospyros mespiliformis", "xh": 0.38}, {"id": "tamarind", "sp": "tamarindus indica", "xh": 0.62, "desc": "A fruiting savanna tree. GloBI records show its pods and leaves eaten by elephants, antelope, warthogs and baboons."}, {"id": "isoberlinia", "sp": "isoberlinia doka", "xh": 0.85}, {"id": "kob", "sp": "kobus kob", "xh": 0.05, "desc": "The most-recorded large herbivore near the park, with about 2,600 counted in 2000. It grazes the floodplain and open savanna.", "ic": "quad"}, {"id": "hartebeest", "sp": "alcelaphus buselaphus", "xh": 0.18, "name": "Hartebeest", "desc": "A grazing antelope of open savanna; about 1,500 western hartebeest were counted in the park in 2000."}, {"id": "warthog", "sp": "phacochoerus africanus", "xh": 0.31, "desc": "A pig 